            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5",
            "treatment.6",
            "treatment.7",
            "treatment.8",
            "treatment.9"
          ],
          "text": "Multi-organ support was provided: the patient was intubated and ventilated, received noradrenaline, and underwent CVVH for acute kidney injury. She underwent four surgical debridements (days 0, 2, 5, and 9), followed by washout, delayed closure, and VAC dressing. A prolonged course of IV piperacillin-tazobactam was given, subsequently tailored to benzylpenicillin and clindamycin per microbiology advice. Prone positioning was performed twice for ARDS. Lines were changed for line sepsis on day 14. Nutrition was provided via nasogastric tube, with improving oral intake thereafter. Renal function recovered and CVVH was discontinued on day 16; the patient was extubated on day 18 and stepped down to the ward on day 24. Wound healing is ongoing by secondary intention with district nurse and tissue viability involvement. Prolonged rehabilitation and physiotherapy have been undertaken.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
