    "compose_patient": {
      "sections": [
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came into hospital with a serious infection of the skin and tissue in your left thigh. This is called a necrotising soft-tissue infection. It caused your body to go into septic shock, which means the infection made you very unwell. You also developed other serious complications, including problems with your lungs, your kidneys, and your heart rhythm."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "We found two types of bacteria in the wound: Group A Streptococcus and anaerobes.\n\nTo support your body, we:\n- Put a breathing tube in and used a machine to help you breathe.\n- Gave you medicines to support your blood pressure.\n- Used a kidney support machine (CVVH) until your kidneys recovered on day 16.\n- Turned you face-down twice to help your lungs.\n- Fed you through a tube into your stomach at first.\n\nYou had four operations to clean the infected tissue (on days 0, 2, 5, and 9). After that, the wound was washed out and closed, and a special wound dressing (VAC dressing) was used.\n\nWe gave you antibiotics through a drip. These were later changed to benzylpenicillin and clindamycin on the advice of our infection specialists.\n\nYou were taken off the breathing machine on day 18 and moved to the ward on day 24. Your wound is still healing, and the district nurse and tissue viability team are involved in your care. You have also been working with physiotherapists and other therapists to help you regain your strength."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "You have the following appointments coming up:\n- Plastics and wound clinic in 2 weeks.\n- Cardiology (heart) clinic in 6 weeks, to check your heart rhythm.\n- A follow-up clinic with the ICU team.\n- Community physiotherapy and occupational therapy will continue at home.\n\nYour GP will check your kidney function and blood pressure after your illness."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
        }
